## Example Interview Summary

I introduced the first CI pipeline for a Node.js backend that had previously been edited and deployed directly on a Linux server.

The main challenge was that the repository was not fully reproducible in a clean environment. I had to standardise npm scripts, adjust the Docker dependency installation process, synchronise the Git branches, verify that no server-side changes were missing from GitHub, and resolve repository authentication issues.

I then created a GitHub Actions workflow that checked out the repository, installed dependencies, and validated the Docker build.

The result was an automated quality gate that detected build problems before deployment and created the foundation for a controlled CD pipeline.
